# The burrow tree PAX carries as /bin/ssh and /bin/burrow-keygen (px104;
# tools/mkburrow builds it, tools/install-burrow installs it).
#
# burrow is an ssh client in wolf (wolffe-lang/burrow, the burrow track):
# OpenSSH-compatible for the profile it speaks (curve25519-sha256,
# ssh-ed25519 host and user keys, chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com, strict
# kex), strict known_hosts checking, publickey login with an unencrypted
# Ed25519 key in OpenSSH's format, one command a session with GIT_PROTOCOL
# by SendEnv: the ssh den's ssh:// and scp-like remotes start. Its clean
# room is the SSH RFCs and OpenSSH's PROTOCOL notes (burrow's README); PAX
# reads no more of its tree than building it needs.
#
# burrow trunk 0d98ce9 (2026-11-06): B0-B4, den over burrow merged
# (burrow#4), pinned in its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.37 /
# lupin 0.1.59 / wolf-std 5b3a5994 (the std the wolf archive bundles).
# tools/mkburrow builds it with THAT toolchain, through burrow's own
# tools/build --static, in two checkouts, refusing two digests. burrow's
# merge gauntlet printed these digests for that build (its check-static
# step), and px104's builds matched them; tools/mkburrow prints whether
# its build does, and holds the two checkouts to each other, not to these
# (the static binary depends on the libc.a it links):
#   burrow         ae0e800f28aef0e1b60c55a38c0d0850587517b34e65ba602cb3649e4361ac43 16326632
#   burrow-keygen  5b21c26c2c22a0a3db6f3210faea0f7c70e7dfdeed4d8775f440e662a5ac2ea2 15480472
BURROW_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/burrow
BURROW_REV=0d98ce92e172d3618b96442319c85bebb42da5b9
